{"agent":"impl-sw-capacity","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`acquire` reserves `need` slots by calling `Slots.hold` once per slot, so a lane can hold a partial set of slots while it waits for the rest. With a GPU pool of `limit=2`, two concurrent lanes using task resource `gpu:2` (`need=2`) and `timeout_s=None` can take different one-slot locks (e.g. slot 0 and slot 1), then each block forever in its second `hold`, waiting for the slot held by the other. The pool-name ordering only orders different pools; it does not make multi-slot acquisition within one pool atomic, and the scheduler’s `busy_counts`/`refusals` are stale before the race reaches `acquire`. The same partial-hold behavior also lets a lane hold slots in an earlier pool while waiting for a later pool, blocking other lanes that need only the earlier pool. This contradicts the stated no-lease/no-hold-while-waiting behavior and violates [r-lock-cycle-selfheal].","digest":"cb4088d42372b9ab","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The source-text guard intended to enforce “no lease” is ineffective. It only rejects the literal substrings `\"import lease\"` and `\"from .. import lease\"`, but a module in `ddflow/services/lanes` can import the lease service as `from ..lease import acquire` (or `import ddflow.services.lease`), and none of those banned substrings appear. Given such a `capacity.py`, the test passes even though capacity may acquire leases while waiting, directly violating [r-lock-cycle-selfheal].","digest":"9657aff676c9d000","location":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test claims to verify that a waiting lane holds no lease, but it only checks that the directory contains `ep-local.0.lock`. Lock files remain after release, so this assertion does not prove the slot is free. If `C.acquire` locks `ep-local.0.lock`, times out, and leaves the lock file descriptor open, the directory still contains exactly `ep-local.0.lock` and the test passes, while `C.busy_counts(pools, tmp_path)` would report `{\"ep-local\": 1}`. The test should assert zero busy count after the outer holder exits; otherwise a leaked lease can pass.","digest":"0f3a30a352e05c66","location":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14424,"diff_sha":"56baa9cb2a7fdd2161ed38f0865385145266bf66dc2e8d6bf675fdcdbc8e1884","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":352.7,"excluded_bytes":3923,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"d7d262ea93892e90","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-capacity.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T201909Z-b92e3e45.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"7711f206bbe400cec1832688d4443b01b703e05e","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 bbfbc51a91d55ccca4cbd63d67b3b42824651bfa","ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py":"100644 04b0b768807892ca5a0bb3bfc118a17ef3185a28","ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py":"100644 0c862ff30ba72bca226771b40efb9217266e64ba","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.lanes.endpoint_slots.toml":"100644 14dc7ea1ee876a33e95eff27be5f6c8490e5a665","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.lanes.slot_wait_s.toml":"100644 f32d781dbd6373d831e7e0ff3a6949e9f75aa104","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golde