{"agent":"impl-sw-capacity","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`acquire` reserves `need` slots by calling `Slots.hold` once per slot, so a lane can hold a partial set of slots while it waits for the rest. With a GPU pool of `limit=2`, two concurrent lanes using task resource `gpu:2` (`need=2`) and `timeout_s=None` can take different one-slot locks (e.g. slot 0 and slot 1), then each block forever in its second `hold`, waiting for the slot held by the other. The pool-name ordering only orders different pools; it does not make multi-slot acquisition within one pool atomic, and the scheduler’s `busy_counts`/`refusals` are stale before the race reaches `acquire`. The same partial-hold behavior also lets a lane hold slots in an earlier pool while waiting for a later pool, blocking other lanes that need only the earlier pool. This contradicts the stated no-lease/no-hold-while-waiting behavior and violates [r-lock-cycle-selfheal].","digest":"cb4088d42372b9ab","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The source-text guard intended to enforce “no lease” is ineffective. It only rejects the literal substrings `\"import lease\"` and `\"from .. import lease\"`, but a module in `ddflow/services/lanes` can import the lease service as `from ..lease import acquire` (or `import ddflow.services.lease`), and none of those banned substrings appear. Given such a `capacity.py`, the test passes even though capacity may acquire leases while waiting, directly violating [r-lock-cycle-selfheal].","digest":"9657aff676c9d000","location":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test claims to verify that a waiting lane holds no lease, but it only checks that the directory contains `ep-local.0.lock`. Lock files remain after release, so this assertion does not prove the slot is free. If `C.acquire` locks `ep-local.0.lock`, times out, and leaves the lock file descriptor open, the directory still contains exactly `ep-local.0.lock` and the test passes, while `C.busy_counts(pools, tmp_path)` would report `{\"ep-local\": 1}`. The test should assert zero busy count after the outer holder exits; otherwise a leaked lease can pass.","digest":"0f3a30a352e05c66","location":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change explicitly implements waiting as a poll: it adds `import time` and documents that “the wait is a bounded poll of the caller’s own process, `timeout_s` long.” This violates [r-lock-cycle-selfheal], which says agents never poll-wait or hold while waiting. A lane calling `capacity.acquire` on a full endpoint/GPU pool will still poll/sleep until the timeout, even if it holds no lease; satisfying the “no lease” half of the rule does not remove the prohibited poll-wait.","digest":"47f6afdefa776ee7","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py: module docstring / acquire wait","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py: module docstring / acquire wait"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Finite `timeout_s` is not enforced as a hard deadline. After a failed sweep the code checks the deadline, then unconditionally sleeps `poll_s`, then retries; if that retry succeeds it yields instead of timing out. For example, with `timeout_s=0.01`, `poll_s=1.0`, and a pool occupied on the first sweep but free on the next, the loop misses, sees the deadline not yet reached, sleeps past the deadline, succeeds on the next sweep, and returns `Held(..., waited_s≈1.0)`. The documented contract “SlotsTimeout when they are not all free after timeout_s” is violated, and a scheduler relying on the timeout can launch a lane after its allowed wait.","digest":"198b753bef14c24c","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"When a sweep misses, `_try_all` discards which pool caused the miss, and the timeout branch always raises for `ordered[0]`. Given two pools `a` and `b` with `a` free and `b` occupied, `timeout_s=0`, `_try_all` takes `a`, fails on `b`, releases `a`, returns `None`, and the timeout branch raises `SlotsTimeout(\"a\", <limit of a>, 0.0)`. The exception names and limits the wrong pool, and it also reports `timeout_s` as the waited time rather than the measured wait, so any scheduler or baseline that uses the exception to identify the saturated pool receives incorrect data.","digest":"ecac00f22ba12a26","location":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test does not actually exercise a lane that is waiting. It calls `C.acquire(pools, 0, tmp_path)` with `timeout_s=0`, so it only covers the immediate-failure path. A `capacity.acquire` implementation that still holds the first free GPU slot while waiting for the second (the prior deadlock scenario with `timeout_s=None`) would pass this test: with timeout `0` it can take one slot, fail to take the other, release the first, and `busy_counts` would still show only the external holder’s one slot. Therefore the test cannot verify the “holds NOTHING meanwhile” property or the two-lane interleaving described in its docstring, leaving the [r-lock-cycle-selfheal] requirement untested.","digest":"f1f79d881b4295d8","location":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_no_hold_while_waiting_two_gpu_lanes","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_no_hold_while_waiting_two_gpu_lanes"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":4,"delta_from":"7711f206bbe400cec1832688d4443b01b703e05e","delta_raised":["47f6afdefa776ee7","198b753bef14c24c","ecac00f22ba12a26","f1f79d881b4295d8"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":8641,"diff_sha":"f2f396de732478c4c289ef35c2275f275294772355025515fd5506c76352f3da","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since 7711f206bb","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":290.4,"family":"alibaba","findings":7,"full_coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"1896792eaa7bf5df","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-capacity.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T204057Z-c0684511.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"2a87c89af4030c806b1a6d8f6c5cd060862921f6","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 bbfbc51a91d55ccca4cbd63d67b3b42824651bfa","ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py":"100644 04b0b768807892ca5a0bb3bfc118a17ef3185a28","ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py":"100644 657aac5a359fc995594c18cdede7666475423e43","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.lanes.endpoint_slots.toml":"100644 14dc7ea1ee876a33e95eff27be5f6c8490e5a665","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.lanes.slot_wait_s.toml":"100644 f32d781dbd6373d831e7e0ff3a6949e9f75aa104","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr":"100644 81452db3849ef1152da024611e6c3b1fa651bb1c","tests/test_lane_capacity.py":"100644 0b024d3d5f5c5880804ea8def34948e678de87d8"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded","tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_wait_holds_no_lease_and_is_bounded","ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py: module docstring / acquire wait","ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","ddflow/services/lanes/capacity.py:acquire","tests/test_lane_capacity.py:test_no_hold_while_waiting_two_gpu_lanes"],"tree_sha":"d5bb1eda5ba6+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},